# Switching to solc 0.8.33 changed the creation code, and so the CREATE2
# address, of Positions and Orders, and which generation a chain runs depends
# on when it was deployed:
#
#   first generation   Ethereum, Arbitrum, Base, Robinhood, Monad, MegaETH
#   second generation  every supported chain except Robinhood
#
# The chains that run only the second generation pin it in their own
# .env.evm.<network> file, which is loaded before this one and wins. This
# shared list is what every other chain falls back to, and it names both
# generations because those chains have both deployed — watching only the
# first would miss anything minted through the second. An address with no code
# on a chain never matches a log, so naming both here is harmless.
LEGACY_ORDERS_V3_ADDRESS="0xfF6cF0Ca6d7a30a60539AcD4bB20B3df84EA0644"
ORDERS_V3_ADDRESS="0x3325428adB409c239E88ca472F50b0efe00E98B4"
